AUDIO: 'And this is where my audit got depressing. 52 of the 100 setups ran the init command once on day one, and never touched the file again. It is a generated summary of the folder structure, and nothing else.'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Nothing about how the humans actually work. So, here is the 10-minute fix. Run {slash} init if you never have. Claude scans your code base and drafts'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the file for you. And it even pulls in rules from an existing agent\'s file or cursor rules. Then, and this is the part 52% of people skip. Edit it.'

[04:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Add the three things the docs say actually matter. Your real build and test commands. Your code style rules. And the two or three architecture facts Claude keeps getting wrong.'

[04:15] [scene:talk]
