AUDIO: 'The official test for every line you add is brutal and perfect. Would removing this line cause Claude to make a mistake? If not, cut it. Mistake two is the opposite disease. The novel.'

[04:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Somewhere around week three, a beginner discovers this file is powerful and starts stuffing everything into it. Coding philosophy. 50 commandments. An entire pasted style guide.'

[04:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The biggest file in my audit was 1,006 lines long. 1,000 lines loaded into every conversation forever. And here is the cruel joke.'

[04:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'More instructions make Claude follow them less. This is straight from the official docs. Keep the file under 200 lines. Because longer files consume more context and reduce adherence.'

[05:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In plain English, a bloated Claude.md means Claude starts ignoring your actual instructions. And you pay tokens for the privilege. Even the creator of Claude code, Boris'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Cherny, says the most common mistake he sees is people over-engineering their configuration. In my 100 setups, 16 were bloated past the line where the docs say adherence drops. And another 11 were so empty they did'

[05:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'nothing at all. Two failure modes, one fix. Keep the main file tight. Push details out. There is an @import syntax that pulls other files in only when needed.'

[05:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And a rules folder where instructions can be scoped to specific paths. So, your database rules only load when Claude actually touches database code. The median across my audit was 90 lines. The sweet spot is real, and it is'

[05:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'smaller than you think. Mistake three, the chatbot habit. This one does not show up in any config file. It shows up in your fingers. Most beginners type into Claude code the'

[06:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'way they type into a chatbot. One vague sentence. Make the dashboard better. Add auth. Fix the bug. Then Claude sprints off,'

[06:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'edits 11 files in a direction you never wanted, and you spend an hour undoing it. Here is the mental switch. You are not chatting. You are delegating.'

[06:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And nobody delegates a project with three words. Claude code has a whole mode built for this. Plan mode. Press shift tab or type {slash} plan, and Claude goes read-only.'

[06:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It explores your code, asks questions, and writes an actual plan of attack. And it cannot touch a single file until you approve. You review the plan, fix the misunderstandings'

