[15:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The docs call it the difference between a session you watch and a session you can walk away from. When Claude can run your tests, it stops being a text generator and becomes a worker that verifies its'

[15:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'own output. And it catches its own bugs before you ever see them. In my audit, 42 of the 100 setups had zero build or test commands in their config.'

[15:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Claude cannot verify anything if you never told it how. Fix two, safety nets. Claude code quietly checkpoints your code at every single prompt. Press escape twice or type {slash} rewind'

[15:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and you can roll the code, the conversation, or both back to any point. But the docs are honest about the limits. Checkpoints do not track everything, and they are not a replacement for version'

[16:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'control. So, small commits every time something works. Do those two things and the horror stories from earlier simply cannot happen to you. Before the recap, a bonus that might'

